<h1>Define Line</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<table class="NormalTable" style="border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0">
<col>
<col>
<tr>
<td valign="top" class="whs4">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../Images/image022.gif" width="203px" height="280px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Capture</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">– for delayed definition of a datum line by probe capture.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US" class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Detect</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">– for interactive detection of a line to selection.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p4"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: Line detection is controlled by <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tolerance</b></span> parameter. See <span lang="EN-GB"><a href="../../References/Preferences_-_Datums_-_Detection_Tolerances.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Datums &gt; Detection Tolerances</a></span> <span lang="EN-GB">for details.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US" class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tolerances</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">– calls</span> <span lang="EN-GB">System&gt;Preferences&gt;Datum&gt;Detection Tolerances</span> <span lang="EN-US">dialog for settings the detection tolerances.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Choose entity</span>:</b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button – to pick an existing normal (of plane, circle, or slot), line, cylinder, or cone axis. The cursor shape for pick mode is</span><img src="../Images/cursor_pick.gif" width="23px" height="24px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt="">.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>extension</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- click and hold down for a while the pick button. The button extension shown below will appear allowing you to select any of the CS axis and use it as line. In this case all line values will be automatically set.</span></p>
<table class="NormalTable" style="margin-left:2px;">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs8">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" valign="top" class="whs9">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../Images/pick_extension.gif" width="71px" height="69px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" valign="top" class="whs11">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../Images/pick_extension_axis.gif" width="71px" height="69px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs8">
<td valign="top" class="whs12">
<p class="normal-table" style="font-style:italic;">Pick button extension</p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs13">
<p class="normal-table" style="font-style:italic;">Pick button with 0X selection</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Listbox</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">– to select from the list a predefined entity (line, cylinder axis or CS axis).</span></p>
<p class="normal-table-func">&#160;</p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Point1, Point2 and Direction:</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>point1 and 2</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">buttons – to pick the start and end points of a line in the viewport.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button for</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>direction</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- to pick an existing normal (of plane or circle), line or cylinder axis.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>extension</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- click and hold down for a while the pick button. The button extension shown above will appear allowing you to select any of the CS axis and use it as direction.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Edit boxes</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">– to type co-ordinates of the start and end points, the direction and the length of the line. As the edit boxes are bent together, the changes in the length will invoke changes in the point2 co-ordinates, for example.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick 2 points</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">– for quick line definition by picking start and end point on the viewport. The c</span>ursor shape for pick N mode is <span style="font-style:italic;"><i><img src="../Images/cursor_pickNline.gif" width="31px" height="31px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt="">.</i></span> To remove a picked point, press the Alt key and click next to the chosen point in the viewport. The <span lang="EN-US">c</span>ursor shape for remove picked point mode is <img src="../Images/cursor_pick_minus.gif" width="20px" height="15px" border="0" class="img_whs15" alt="">.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="sub-head">Temporary Line</p>
<p>When all <span lang="EN-US">values are set the new line will be visualised in the viewport as temporary entity. There are different types of temporary lines:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>temporary construction line</b></span> - when a <span lang="EN-US">line</span> takes part in other entity definition, it appears in the viewport as temporary construction datum (white/black coloured by default). Its appearance can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Temporary Construction Datum</b></i></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>current construction line</b></span> - the currently edited/selected <span lang="EN-US">line</span> appears in the viewport as highlighted temporary datum (light red by default). Its colour can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Highlighted</b></i></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span>: If the temporary construction datum is currently edited, it appears as highlighted temporary datum.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>final construction line</b></span> - when all definition fields/all construction tabs are filled, then the <span lang="EN-US">line</span> appears in the viewport as final construction datum (green/black coloured by default). Its appearance can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Final Construction Datum.</b></i></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p3"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span>: If the current construction datum is actually the final one, then it will be coloured as final construction datum.</p>
<p>When this final construction datum is really created then its colour will be changed to the real datum colour (set in <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b><a href="../../References/Display_Settings-Colours.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours</a></b></i></span> ).</p>
<p class="Warning">The line direction is indicated by an arrow and by the movement of the points on it.</p>
